/**
 * A2UISurfaceRenderer Component
 *
 * In-IDE Chat Runner Surface Renderer for the A2UI (Agent-to-User Interface v0.9.1) Protocol.
 * Provides interactive rendering of A2UI surfaces generated by agents, supporting:
 * - Parsing A2UI v0.9.1 message streams (createSurface, updateComponents, updateDataModel, deleteSurface)
 * - Auto-wrapping standalone A2UI component JSON blocks, Vega-Lite specs, and GoogleMap payloads
 * - Flattening nested inline component children and rendering multi-root component lists
 * - Reactive local state management for surface component trees and data models
 * - Two-way data binding for input widgets (/selectedWarehouse, /transferQuantity, /adjustedPrice, /form/...)
 * - Dynamic JSON pointer resolution and context interpolation on user action dispatch
 * - Rich visual rendering for Material 3, Gemini Enterprise Composite, and Basic catalog widgets:
 *   - MaterialCard, Column, Row, GridList, ExpansionPanel / Accordion (collapsible), Tabs (interactive), Text, Banner
 *   - MaterialBadge, MaterialIcon, MaterialProgressBar, MaterialProgressSpinner, MaterialDivider, MaterialTable, RichTable, DataTable
 *   - MaterialInput / TextInput / NumberInput / TextArea, MaterialSelect / Dropdown, MaterialSlider, MaterialCheckbox, MaterialSlideToggle / Switch
 *   - MaterialButton / MaterialButtonToggle with resolved action context dispatch
 *   - VegaChart / VegaLiteChart / InteractiveChart with visual bar, arc/donut, and trend previews + collapsible Vega-Lite v5 spec inspector
 *   - GoogleMap with interactive cartographic SVG map canvas, plotted lat/lng pins, zoom controls, and marker inspector
 *   - MosaicCarousel & MosaicSlideCard with hero images (plus automatic SVG illustration fallback), prev/next controls, and slide indicators
 *
 * Architectural Decisions:
 * 1. Reactive JSON Pointer Model: Local component inputs mutate surface dataModel via RFC 6901 pointers.
 * 2. Deferred Action Context Resolution: Button click events resolve pointer references in action.event.context
 *    against current dataModel values before emitting onUserAction.
 * 3. 8pt Grid System: All padding, margins, gaps, and sizes strictly adhere to multiples of 8px.
 *
 * @author Mike Nimer <mikenimer@google.com>
 */

